# Chaining

```java
if (A) {
  ...
}
else if (B) {
  ...
}
else if (C) {
  ...
}
else {
  ...
}
```

* There is no limit to how long you can chain the else/ifs
* Always try to think about how to condense long chains
* optionally ends in a `else`. if it ends in an `else` you are saying that there is a case that something will happen or you will lose points.
* Runs checking `A->B->C1...` So ORDER MATTERS.
